/** In the Jack language, arrays are implemented as instances of 
the OS class Array. 
Once declared, the array elements can be accessed using the syntax arr[i]. 
Jack arrays are not typed: each array element can hold a primitive 
data type or an object type, and different elements in the same array 
can have different types. */
class Array{
    /** Constructs a new array of the given size.*/
    function Array new(int size){
        return Memory.alloc(size); 
    }

    /** Disposes this array.*/
    method void dispose(){
        do Memory.deAlloc(this);
        return;
    }
}